getHTMLCode [SimTalk] - Frame
Returns the contents of the Frame designated by <Path> as HTML code of a pixel-based graphic and
assigns it to the passed parameters.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.getHTMLCode([Caption:string, Width:integer, Height:integer, 
SizeInPercent:string, CameraPositionX:real, CameraPositionY:real, 
CameraPositionZ:real, CameraRotationX:real, CameraRotationZ:real, 
CameraRotationX:real, CameraRotationZ:real]) → string
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The optional parameter Caption of data type string designates the desired caption of the graphic. If you
specify the caption, Plant Simulation shows the graphic with this caption.
• The optional parameter Width of data type integer designates the desired Width of the graphic.
If you do not specify the Width and the Height, Plant Simulation uses the width and the height of the 2D
view or of the 3D view respectively in which all objects contained in the Frame are visible.
• The optional parameter Height of data type integer designates the desired Height of the graphic.
If you do not specify the Width and the Height, Plant Simulation uses the width and the height of the 2D
view or of the 3D view respectively in which all objects contained in the Frame are visible.
• The optional parameter SizeInPercent of data type string designates the desired size of the graphic in
percent, for example "75%". You can specify the percentage instead of the parameters for the Width
and the Height.
• The optional parameter CameraPositionX of data type real designates the x-axis of the camera position.
• The optional parameter CameraPositionY of data type real designates the y-axis of the camera position.
• The optional parameter CameraPositionZ of data type real designates the z-axis of the camera position.
You only have to specify the optional parameters for the CameraPosition if you also specify the optional
parameters for the CameraRotation.
• The optional parameter CameraRotationX of data type real designates the rotation of the camera
around the x-axis.
• The optional parameter CameraRotationZ of data type real designates the rotation of the camera
around the z-axis.
getHTMLCode [SimTalk] - Frame
Plant Simulation Help 11-1519
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

You can also use the optional parameters for the CameraRotation without specifying the
CameraPosition.
If you specify the optional parameters for the CameraPosition and/or CameraRotation, you also have to
specify the parameters for the Width and the Height or for the SizeInPercent.
Return Value
The return value has the data type string.
Examples
print MyFrame.getHTMLCode
MyFrame.getHTMLCode("Caption")
MyFrame.getHTMLCode(100, 100) // size in mm
MyFrame.getHTMLCode("Caption", 100, 100) // caption and size in mm
MyFrame.getHTMLCode("75%")
// size in percent of the graphic showing all objects
MyFrame.getHTMLCode(*)
// as big as necessary to show all objects and shown as big as possible in 
the HtmlReport
MyFrame.getHTMLCode(100,*)
// width in mm, height proportional calculated from the size required to 
show all objects
MyFrame.getHTMLCode(*, 100)
// height in mm, width proportional calculated from the size required to 
show all objects
MyFrame.getHTMLCode(100%, -1.123, 2.345, -3.456, -45.0, 15.0)
// 100% of the size of the graphic showing all objects while specifying 
CameraPosition and CameraRotation
See also
Display a Frame
Display a HtmlReport
